                <pb facs="0173" n="101" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg101"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 774/584.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Bishop Brent.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1909-02-26"><hi rendition="#italic">February 26,
                        1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Bacon informs him that department is gratified with resolutions passed by
                    international commission, authorizes him to publish resolutions, and compliments
                    him on the successful termination of this phase of his work.</p>
            </div>
